{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You give</b> — Jacob is our father for all of us alone, for no other nations intermingle with us; therefore it is written, \"the God of Israel.\" \"Our father for all of us\" — and he did not mention Isaac, for he is also the father of Edom. And because Abraham was the first to call on the name of HaShem, turning away from his close forefathers, and HaShem cut a covenant with him first, therefore he mentioned Abraham and had no need to mention Isaac. And the meaning: You give Your truth to Jacob — and what is it? That which You swore to our fathers from days of old."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:19.650439442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}